# Search in controllers (PRG)

## Plugin semantics

Search commonly uses Post/Redirect/Get friendly filtering so filter state lives in the query string for pagination. Controllers should apply search to the query then paginate — not rebuild filters inline.

## Required behavior

- Follow neighboring controllers for Search component / `searchManager` / `find('search')` patterns used in this app.
- Keep filter definitions on the Table; controllers pass request params into the search find.
- Preserve pagination compatibility with filtered query strings.

## Anti-patterns

- POST-only filter handling that breaks pagination bookmarks without project convention
- Copying Table filter logic into the controller
